// The approval gate written against the ATTEMPT -- the weak form, and the conventional one.
//
// This reads as an approval gate and is not one. AgentCore records a `request` event for EVERY
// attempt, permitted or not, so what this actually requires is that somebody TRIED to get an
// approval. A sequence of refusals opens it exactly as a granted approval would, which hands the
// caller the capability the approval existed to protect.
//
// It is not a strawman: `::request` appears in 555 policy files across Dogwood's own corpus
// against `::response`'s 94, so this is the shape an author reaches for first.
//
// tests/strands/dogwood_replay.py gives this file and approval_gate_response.dw the same denied
// approval and asks the real engine. It returns ALLOW here and DENY there.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Anchor::Action::"Trade",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1000s Anchor::Action::"Approve"::request{ }
};
